preConditionHook:
// NumBarsIfBelowProfitThreshold -- Grimes A list (G08-19 / G10-04, key
// NumBarsIfBelowProfitThreshold). Authored 2026-09-22 as a new profitThreshold
// input on NumBarsIfLosing and split out as its own rule 2026-11-07, because the
// 202608 BAS and 202611 BRK and OWN templates place NumBarsIfLosing, so that
// rule stays exactly as those families run it. Code otherwise unchanged.
//
// The general time stop -- "if a trade does not hit some predetermined profit
// limit within a certain time, exit": the position has been open numBars bars
// or more and open profit is still strictly below profitThreshold. It is
// NumBarsIfLosing with the 0 in the profit test promoted to an input, so at
// profitThreshold 0 this is NumBarsIfLosing exactly. Grimes's failure-test
// reading is numBars 4 with profitThreshold =
// riskMultiple * stopDistance * BigPointValue. He gives no number for the
// general form; the default profitThreshold(100) follows the corpus's currency
// convention (TrailArmedAfterProfitThreshold's armProfitDollars(100)), not a
// value from the book. The grid keeps numBars >= 1, since BarsSinceEntry is 0
// while flat.
//
// THE COMPARISON IS STRICT, as in NumBarsIfLosing. The merged note wanted "at
// or below"; el_lt is kept so that profitThreshold 0 reproduces NumBarsIfLosing
// character for character, and the boundary case is a tick of profit either
// way.
//
// UNITS: profitThreshold is ACCOUNT CURRENCY, because ctx.OpenPositionProfit()
// is (VERIFIED: close-marked, net of the ENTRY SIDE's commission, slippage and
// accrued swap -- one side, not the round turn). A threshold in price points
// or ATRs is FlatTradeScratchExit, a different rule.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 0.
